      "writtenOn": "2024-11-26T02:38:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I added the definitions of alternative_has_cap_likely() and alternative_has_cap_unlikely() during the forward-port to android14-6.1.  I forgot the details, but I must have run into a build error that was resolved by adding them.  Indeed, if I try removing them on this branch (android16-6.12), I get the following error:\n\n```\narch/arm64/include/asm/mmu.h:61:9: error: call to undeclared function \u0027alternative_has_cap_unlikely\u0027; ISO C99 and later do not support implicit function declarations [-Wimplicit-function-declaration]\n   61 |         return alternative_has_cap_unlikely(ARM64_UNMAP_KERNEL_AT_EL0);\n      |                ^\n```\n\nI don\u0027t remember why I made it return true for LDAPR et al.  It does sound like it should return false instead.  I\u0027ve changed this function to return false unconditionally, and fips140.ko still works.",
      "parentUuid": "e71862a2_4bf3ae12",
      "revId": "e5cdc811be1a51de26d311b9534029b53905256a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
